  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 954 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nTemperatures for the rest of the evening will be in the mid to\nupper 40s around El Paso, and closer to the low 40s outside the\nmetropolitan area. Temperatures will rise to the low to mid 70s on\nWednesday, at or around seasonal normals for early November. Winds\nwill increase from the west to about 10-15 mph as an upper-level\nlow passes through the Four Corners. This upper-level low will\nbring a Pacific cold front that will cool temperatures down\novernight and into Thursday.\n\nConditions for the rest of the week will be dry and quiet, though\nan upper level trough moving through the Desert Southwest around\nFriday/Saturday could bring some limited moisture and rain\nchances. The ECMWF has a cutoff low splitting off from the trough\nSaturday afternoon, while the GFS does not. It remains to be seen\nhow much precipitation we'll see.",
